<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Mac FALLBACK scanner. The 24/7 primary scan runs in the cloud (GitHub Actions,
  every 2h at :00 UTC) but its datacenter IP is tarpitted/blocked by several CZ
  sites. This LaunchAgent runs the scan from the Mac's residential IP for exactly
  those hard sources (SCAN_SOURCES below), so when the Mac is on they get covered.

  Overlap with the cloud run DOES happen. The :40 slot was chosen assuming the
  cloud run starts at :00 and ends inside 30 min, but GitHub's cron drifts by
  1.8-4.5 h (measured 2026-09-03: a cloud run started 10:29, ran 26 min and
  finished at 10:51 — 11 min AFTER this job's 10:40 run). What keeps the overlap
  survivable is per-source scoping, not timing: markMissedOffers is strictly
  per-source (this subset never deactivates cloud-scanned sources) and
  notifications_log dedups sends. A same-source race between the two processes
  remains possible for the sources both still scan; treat :40 as a best-effort
  offset, not a guarantee.

  Sleep is NOT handled by launchd coalescing alone. StartCalendarInterval merges
  slots missed during a FULL sleep into one catch-up run on wake, but macOS also
  wakes every ~15 min for 2-45 s (DarkWake, `pmset -g log`, 2026-09-03) and
  launchd happily fires this job inside such a window: the Mac sleeps seconds
  later, the process freezes mid-fetch, its sockets die, and on thaw every slow
  source reports "fetch exceeded 420000ms budget" — 4 of 5 night runs that day,
  ~57 % of Mac runs over 7 days. The scan now detects a frozen fetch phase
  (src/core/sleep-watch.ts, 60 s threshold) and DISCARDS the run: status
  'skipped' for every source, nothing written to source_runs, nothing ingested,
  nothing sent, exit 0. A slept-through slot therefore costs one skipped run,
  not a false `failed` row. DB + Telegram creds come from .env.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>com.daniel.dovolenky.scan</string>

	<key>ProgramArguments</key>
	<array>
		<string>/bin/zsh</string>
		<string>-lc</string>
		<string>cd '/Users/daniel/Library/CloudStorage/OneDrive-Osobní/Effistream/dovolenky' &amp;&amp; mkdir -p logs data &amp;&amp; SCAN_SOURCES='fischer,eximtours,etravel,firo,dovolenkovani,bluestyle,zajezdy,dovolena' /usr/bin/env npx tsx src/cli/scan.ts >> logs/scan.log 2>&amp;1</string>
	</array>

	<key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<key>Hour</key>
			<integer>0</integer>
			<key>Minute</key>
			<integer>40</integer>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<key>Hour</key>
			<integer>2</integer>
			<key>Minute</key>
			<integer>40</integer>
		</dict>
